cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the archived release and the manuscript below."
title: "Noise-generator bias in temporally correlated ballistic deposition"
abstract: >-
  Simulation and analysis code for a numerical study of (1+1)-dimensional ballistic
  deposition driven by noise with long-range temporal correlations. The work shows that
  Mandelbrot's fast fractional Gaussian noise, the generator used throughout the published
  literature on this problem, is discontinuous at zero correlation exponent, so the family
  never samples the short-range Kardar-Parisi-Zhang regime; and that the standard
  fixed-significance onset construction cannot locate the crossover when the detection floor
  depends on system size. No measured theta_c is reported.
